1. Definitions and Scope

"Licensor" means Nankai University. An authorized representative may act for
the Licensor only within the scope of its written authorization.

"You" and "Your" mean the individual or legal entity exercising the
permissions or accepting the obligations in this license. A person accepting
for an entity must have authority to bind that entity.

"Software" means the original source code, scripts, configuration files,
documentation, examples, and Project Model Weights distributed with this
license, but only to the extent that the Licensor owns or is authorized to
license them. Excluded materials are described in section 6. This license
applies to the version distributed with it and does not change rights
validly granted under any earlier or separate license.

"Project Model Weights" means original RSSNet model weights and checkpoints
supplied by the Licensor with this license, to the extent that the Licensor
owns or is authorized to license the relevant rights. Materials identified
as third-party materials or supplied under a separate license are excluded.
Merely hosting or linking to weights does not make them Project Model
Weights.

"Research Model" means a model, including its weights and checkpoints,
created through any of the following activities undertaken in reliance on
the permissions in this license:
  (a) using Software or Modifications as part of its training or fine-tuning
      pipeline to compute or update that model's parameters;
  (b) incorporating, initializing from, adapting, or fine-tuning Project
      Model Weights or an existing Research Model; or
  (c) deliberately using Software, Modifications, Project Model Weights, or
      a Research Model to generate teacher targets, pseudo-labels, or
      intermediate features specifically to train that model, including
      through distillation, whether generation and training are simultaneous
      or performed in separate stages.
Later versions that retain or adapt such parameters, including pruned,
quantized, or merged versions, and models produced by the activities above
using a Research Model, remain Research Models.

A model is not a Research Model merely because it is compared with RSSNet,
is evaluated using RSSNet without training or adapting its parameters, is
discussed in the same publication, or follows ideas described in a paper.
Ordinary inference outputs, spectra, measurements, figures, tables, and
publications are not themselves Research Models. Using independently
available ordinary research outputs as data does not by itself make another
model a Research Model; paragraph (c) applies to deliberate generation of
training signals for that model, not incidental reuse of such outputs.

A genuinely independent retraining is outside this definition if it uses
independently implemented training code, does not incorporate or adapt
Software, Project Model Weights, or Research Model parameters, and does not
use the teacher targets, pseudo-labels, or intermediate features described
in paragraph (c) for that retraining. Merely resetting parameters while
continuing to train with the Software is not independent retraining. This
exclusion does not waive any independently applicable patent, data, or
third-party rights.

"Modification" means a modification, adaptation, translation, or derivative
work that incorporates copyright-protected expression from the Software. An
independent implementation does not become a Modification merely because it
uses similar ideas, methods, mathematical concepts, or algorithms.

"Academic Non-Commercial Use" means personal academic study, teaching,
scientific research, reproduction or evaluation of research results, and
preparation of academic publications by individuals, educational
institutions, or non-profit research institutions, solely for academic or
educational purposes and not for Commercial Use.

Receiving an ordinary academic salary, stipend, scholarship, government
research grant, or non-profit research grant does not by itself make a use
commercial. The actual purpose and activities must still satisfy this
license. A university affiliation or publication of results does not by
itself make a use non-commercial.

"Commercial Use" includes:
  (a) use by or on behalf of a commercial business for its research,
      development, evaluation, internal operations, or other business needs;
  (b) development, incorporation, testing, or deployment of the Software or
      Modifications in a commercial product, device, model, or service;
  (c) paid analysis, consulting, outsourced development, or commissioned
      technical work for a commercial purpose;
  (d) selling, renting, leasing, or commercially distributing the Software
      or Modifications, or providing their functionality as a commercial
      hosted service, API, platform, or subscription; and
  (e) using the Software or Modifications to train, test, operate, or improve
      a model intended for commercial use.
A person's employment by a business does not by itself make genuinely
independent personal academic study commercial; work undertaken for that
business's needs remains within paragraph (a). Industrial quality control
and paid contract analysis for commercial purposes are examples of
Commercial Use. A hospital or other non-profit affiliation does not itself
authorize clinical or operational use: use outside Academic Non-Commercial
Use requires separate permission even if it is not profit-making.

These activities require separate permission whether or not the Software
itself is sold or supplied to customers. Research commissioned or funded by
a commercial business also requires separate written permission unless the
Licensor expressly confirms in writing that the specific research is
permitted under this license.

