make this license available and prominently identify the
later-commercial-use restriction, onward-transfer and citation conditions,
liability limits, and choice of law and court. Provide a reasonable
opportunity to read the terms and request an explanation. Do not use a
preselected acceptance box or infer express acceptance from silence.

For a model creator, an express acceptance identifying the creator and this
version may be sent to the project contact in section 5, or recorded through
a license-acceptance facility provided by the Licensor or an authorized
distributor. For a model recipient, acceptance may be recorded by the
transferor. Retain the accepted terms, version, affirmative acknowledgment,
and sufficient information to identify the accepting party and date, in
accordance with applicable privacy and record-retention law. Express
acceptance is not a commercial permission request and requires no separate
commercial approval for otherwise permitted academic activities. A
recipient's acceptance does not validate a transferor's ownership or cure
missing third-party permissions.

