  (g) do not impose additional legal or technical restrictions on recipients'
      exercise of the permissions expressly granted in the covered Software
      or Modifications. This does not expand their rights or displace the
      acceptance requirements in section 2.2 and separate third-party terms.

Redistribution must be free of license fees or profit. You may recover only
actual, reasonable physical-media and delivery costs, without a markup. This
narrow cost-recovery exception is not Commercial Use by itself and does not
authorize charging for software access, hosted functionality, consulting,
training, or analysis services.

An inaccessible or renamed source repository does not waive attribution:
retain the project name and the source URL supplied with the received
version, and add a verified successor URL if known. A repository host or
