6. Third-Party Materials, Data, and Model Weights

This license does not relicense third-party code, dependencies, spectral
libraries, datasets, pretrained model weights, papers, or other materials
that the Licensor does not own or have authority to license.

The original RRUFF and UNIPR spectral libraries and third-party model
weights are outside this license. The project-generated RRUFF-2Mix and
UNIPR-2Mix datasets are also outside this software license; their status as
project-generated datasets does not establish unrestricted rights in the
underlying spectra. Use and redistribution of each dataset require its
separately applicable permission, including any upstream conditions. This
license supplies no dataset permission merely because a dataset is hosted
in, linked from, or described as available with the project.

Project Model Weights, as defined in section 1, are included in sections 2
and 3; weights supplied under separate terms remain subject to those terms.
A claim that weights were trained by the project does not override
applicable rights or restrictions in training materials. Permission to use
generation scripts does not itself grant permission to use or redistribute
their input data or generated datasets.

See DATASETS.md, if supplied, for dataset-specific permission and access
information available with the release. A distribution containing dataset
files must identify their source and applicable permission in DATASETS.md or
an equivalent accompanying dataset notice. Unconfirmed permissions must not
be represented as granted. If no applicable permission is identified, this
software license supplies none. Code availability does not guarantee
permission or access to every dataset used in a publication.

Distributions must preserve applicable third-party license and attribution
notices and identify included separately licensed materials in a NOTICE or
equivalent accompanying record, with their source and applicable terms. Such
a record documents permissions; it cannot create missing permissions. Any
included paper, website asset, or dependency retains its own applicable
terms. Merely listing a dependency does not resolve license compatibility;
compatibility must be assessed for the actual incorporation and
distribution.

Separate licenses and notices for those materials continue to apply.
Distribution of the Software does not override any party's obligations to
