7. Academic Publications, Results, Research Models, and Attribution

7.1 Mandatory citation for public research publications

You may publish research results obtained through permitted use of the
Software, subject to any independently applicable rights in included
materials and the following citation condition.

If you publicly publish a paper, thesis, dissertation, report, benchmark, or
other scholarly work reporting results obtained using the Software,
Modifications, or Research Models, you must acknowledge RSSNet and cite:

Gaoruishu Long, Jinchao Liu, Bo Liu, Jie Liu, and Xiaolin Hu.
A Brain-Inspired Deep Separation Network for Single Channel Raman Spectra Unmixing.
arXiv:2604.22324, 2026. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2604.22324

This citation and acknowledgement requirement is a condition of the
permissions granted by this license. Use the publication venue's normal
citation format, identifying the paper by its title and authors, and include
the arXiv identifier or DOI above. A verified final published citation to
the same paper may be used instead. Citation details in README.md or
CITATION.cff may be used. If those files are missing or incomplete, the
authors, title, year, and arXiv identifier above suffice. Acknowledgement of
RSSNet may be included in the methods, acknowledgements, or other
appropriate part of the publication. No acknowledgement of endorsement or
attribution of coauthorship is required.

Private study, unpublished experiments, and internal research notes do not
require a formal paper citation. Retention of notices on redistribution is
separately required by section 3. Omissions are subject to section 10.

