7.3 Research Model use and onward transfer

By expressly accepting the Research Model Terms, You agree to use Research
Models created or received under them only for Academic Non-Commercial Use
unless You first obtain separate written authorization from the Licensor or
its duly authorized representative. Later commercial deployment, sale,
licensing for commercial use, or use in a commercial product or service
requires that authorization even if the model was originally created solely
for academic research and the later activity no longer uses or includes the
Software. The commercial activities in section 1 apply equally to Research
Models. Genuinely independent retraining that satisfies the exclusion in
section 1 is not subject to this contractual Research Model restriction;
separate patent and third-party rights remain.

You may share a Research Model for Academic Non-Commercial Use if You:
  (a) identify the model, its version or checkpoint, its RSSNet-related
      origin, and the model transferor;
  (b) supply a Research Model Notice stating that the Research Model
      Terms of RSSNet License version 1.4 apply, highlighting the
      later-commercial-use, citation, onward-transfer, liability, and
      law-and-court terms, and providing a complete copy of this license
      or a durable, accessible reference to that exact version; and
  (c) obtain and retain the recipient's express acceptance as specified
      in section 2.2 before transferring the model.
Supply a complete copy of the license on request or if the referenced copy
is inaccessible. The notice must distinguish the model transferor's own
rights from the Licensor's rights; it must not label independently owned
model weights as Software solely because this section applies. If a model
contains Software or Modifications, section 3 also requires the complete
license and relevant notices to accompany their distribution. The same
conditions apply to subsequent transfers. The physical-media and delivery
cost exception in section 3 also applies to these academic transfers.

A Research Model Notice is not a substitute for assent. Publicly posting an
unrestricted download with a notice alone does not satisfy paragraph (c).
The notice and acceptance must not falsely claim that the Licensor owns
independently created model weights or has granted third-party permissions.
A separate written agreement may expressly replace these conditions for the
activities it authorizes.

These conditions are contractual obligations of persons who accept them.
They do not create copyright or patent rights where none exist or
automatically bind a person who has not agreed to them. They do not apply
retroactively to models created or received without reliance on this license
and without acceptance of these conditions. Statutory rights and separate
permissions remain unaffected. Subject to mandatory applicable law, agreed
Research Model use, citation, and onward-transfer obligations survive
termination for models created or received under these terms. Survival of
obligations does not itself continue a terminated copyright or patent
permission. The effect on continued model use and reinstatement is stated in
section 10.3. The warranty, liability, dispute, and accrued-rights
provisions also survive to the extent relevant to those activities.

